// SB+failed-cas.
//
// SB+cas with CASes that fail.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: Coherence allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     SC forbids. SC forbids SB, and a fence adds no behaviour.
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     TSO forbids. Equivalent to x86-TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to x86-TSO (zoo edge).
//   the models' definitions:
//     x86-TSO forbids. A failing lock cmpxchg still drains the store buffer:
//       the lock prefix, not the write, is the barrier (Sewell et al.,
//       x86-TSO).
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: RC11, RC11z, RC17,
//     OD-LSO, MRD, CC, PC, PRAM, Causal, Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, MW,
//     WFR. RA, SRA and WRA are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and
//     this program has other accesses.
x := 0; y := 0; z := 0; w := 0;
{
  rpz := &z;
  x := 1;
  rz := CAS(rlx, rlx, rpz, 5, 1);
  r0 := y
} ||| {
  rpw := &w;
  y := 1;
  rw := CAS(rlx, rlx, rpw, 5, 1);
  r1 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 0 && r1 = 0) [Coherence]
forbid (r0 = 0 && r1 = 0) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO]
